From 1cd8dbc0171e53226ba9171c7c492570558c6f43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meng Li <Meng.Li@windriver.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2025 22:29:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] t23x: overlay: create dts for booting NVIDIA Orin Nano
 platform directly

So far, NVIDIA Yocto SDK only supports for loading dtb from configuration
table of uefi firmware. The reason as below:
During deploying images onto board, the NVIDIA burn script concatenates
that basic dtb and overlay dtbo files one by one at the end of uefi with
4k bytes alignment. During booting system, uefi image gets the dtb and
dtbo files, and then create a full feature dtb, and then modify some dts
node based on specific board, and then register it into configuration
table. When kernel boots up, the full feature dtb will be passed into
kernel. Based on this kind of booting mode, it needs to spend on more
than 20 minutes to burn the whole sysyem image even if user wants to
update kernel image and dtb. It is very inconvinent and unacceptable to
burn the whole system image during debugging kernel and dtb. Therefore,
in order to solve this issue, create dts used to improve that it is able
to be used to boot kernel directly.
Because the Nano platform is the low performance one of Orin series,
it needs to remove some nodes so that the final dtb is compatible with
Nano platform. In order to discard the node dependence during removing
dts nodes, add the '-f' parameter to generate dtb forcedly.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Meng Li <Meng.Li@windriver.com>
---
